+     * method's loop, line for line, but for these:
+     *
+     * <ul>
+     * <li><b>Settled.</b> After each round, an active alternative whose first
+     *     {@link Anytime#RACE_FROM} paired differences with Forge's answer are exactly
+     *     the same ({@link Anytime#settled}) gets no more rollouts at this horizon.
+     *     The shallow rounds go to the unsettled, unraced alternatives (pruned to the
+     *     budget among themselves, raced as today), with Forge's answer rolled only
+     *     while one of them is left.  The settled test runs before the race, so an
+     *     alternative the race retires the round it settles can still be deepened.</li>
+     * <li><b>Deepened.</b> A settled alternative whose shallow difference is at least
+     *     {@code -margin} is deepened, and gets a deep leg only where the verdict can
+     *     still move ({@link Anytime#deepLegs}: the shallow best if it is a deepened
+     *     winner, then the deepened near-ties; none while the shallow best is an
+     *     unsettled winner).  A round's deep legs roll Forge's answer once, then those
+     *     alternatives, at {@code horizon + 1} with the round's seed.  <b>Shallow first</b>: a round runs deep legs only when it starts with no
+     *     shallow work left ({@link Anytime#deepThisRound}); {@code deepmix=1} runs them
+     *     in every round, after its shallow legs.  A deepened comparison stops at
+     *     {@link Anytime#DEEP_MIN} settled deep pairs, {@code maxrounds} deep pairs, or
+     *     its second deep error.</li>
+     * <li><b>The verdict.</b> The shallow rule's (the margin rule on {@link Anytime#best})
+     *     is kept as {@link Report#shallowChosen}; each deepened alternative gets
+     *     {@link Anytime#deepVerdict}; the index played is {@link Anytime#deepChoice}.</li>
+     * </ul>
+     *
+     * A deep rollout has the decision's own deadline; one the deadline cuts returns
+     * null, counts in {@code .deepen.cut} alone, ends the loop and never feeds a
+     * verdict.  A deep error never moves the shallow search.  Every shallow statistic
+     * keeps its meaning: {@code timedOut} is set only when the deadline cut shallow
+     * work, and {@code search.rollouts}, {@code search.playUs} and the report's
+     * {@code playouts} count shallow rollouts only, a deep rollout's own counters going
+     * under {@code search.<k>.deepen.} ({@code deepSink}).  Deep counters, by kind:
+     * {@code settled}, {@code pairs}, {@code decisions}, {@code rollouts},
+     * {@code playUs}, {@code copyUs}, {@code rounds}, {@code cut}, {@code errors},
+     * {@code short}, {@code starved}, {@code shallowCut}, {@code vetoes},
+     * {@code promotions} and {@code changed} (D542 point 7).
